d diet therapy. He has authored an update on probiotics, prebiotics, and symbiotics in clinical nutrition, showcasing his expertise in these areas. Additionally, he has contributed to a manual that addresses nutritional needs across different life stages, further emphasizing his commitment to advancing knowledge in nutrition. Olveira Fuster G also serves as an editor and contributor to the book titled \"Dietoterapia, nutrición clínica y metabolismo,\" which reflects his comprehensive understanding of clinical nutrition and metabolism. Through these works, Olveira Fuster G has established himself as a key figure in the literature surrounding nutritional requirements and diet therapy.", "DIETA EQUILIBRADA:\"DIETA EQUILIBRADA\" refers to a balanced diet that is crucial for maintaining overall health and preventing chronic diseases. It encompasses a variety of foods consumed in appropriate proportions, which is essential not only for general well-being but also for specific health management, such as preventing kidney stones. A balanced diet provides all the necessary nutrients required for optimal health and serves as a foundational aspect of nutritional education, highlighting its importance in disease prevention and health maintenance.", "FIBRA DIETÉTICA:FIBRA DIETÉTICA refers to dietary fiber, a crucial component of nutrition that plays a significant role in promoting digestive health. It is found in various food sources, including whole grains, legumes, vegetables, and fruits. Dietary fiber aids in digestion, helps stabilize blood sugar levels, and contributes to the reduction of energy density in foods, which can promote feelings of fullness and assist in weight control.\n\nResearch indicates that dietary fiber is particularly beneficial for the elderly, as it is linked to improved overall health. Additionally, it is essential for children's diets, supporting their digestive health. As a type of carbohydrate that the body cannot digest, dietary fiber is important for gut health and is associated with various health benefits, including the potential to inhibit the absorption of adenine, which may lower uric acid levels.\n\nFIBRA DIETÉTICA is recognized in dietary recommendations and guidelines, such as those from the World Health Organization (WHO), emphasizing its importance in maintaining a balanced and healthy diet.", "RECOMENDACIONES DE INGESTA:Las recomendaciones de ingesta son pautas establecidas por organizaciones de salud para asegurar una nutrición adecuada en la población.", "TRASTORNOS POR DÉFICIT DE YODO:Los trastornos por déficit de yodo son condiciones de salud que resultan de una ingesta insuficiente de yodo, afectando la función tiroidea.", "FEDERACIÓN ESPAÑOLA DE SOCIEDADES DE ALIMENTACIÓN, NUTRICIÓN Y DIETÉTICA:The Federación Española de Sociedades de Alimentación, Nutrición y Dietética (FESNAD) is an organization that provides consensus on dietary fats and oils for the adult Spanish population.", "INSTITUTE OF MEDICINE:The Institute of Medicine (IOM) is a nonprofit organization that operates as part of the National Academy of Sciences. It is dedicated to providing expert advice on health and medicine to decision-makers and the public. The IOM offers a wide range of services, including the development of clinical guidelines, nutritional guidelines, and dietary reference intakes for various nutrients. It focuses on delivering evidence-based information regarding health and nutrition, which encompasses dietary recommendations and requirements. Additionally, the IOM defines adequate fiber intake during pregnancy and lactation, ensuring that its health recommendations and guidelines are grounded in scientific evidence. Overall, the Institute of Medicine plays a crucial role in shaping health policy and providing comprehensive health recommendations, including those related to dietary intake.", "LUENGO PÉREZ LM:Luengo Pérez LM is an author who contributed to the manual on nutrition in different life stages.", "BEATO VÍBORA P:Beato Víbora P is an author who contributed to the manual on nutrition in different life stages.", "NICOLÁS BLANCO M:Nicolás Blanco M is an author who contributed to the manual on nutrition in different life stages.", "METABOLISMO:Metabolismo encompasses all biochemical processes that occur within living organisms to maintain life, including essential functions such as digestion, nutrient absorption, and the conversion of food into energy. It is closely related to nutrition and exercise, playing a crucial role in understanding the nutritional needs of individuals, particularly during specific conditions such as pregnancy, obesity, and recovery from burns or severe trauma. The metabolic processes are vital for sustaining life and can be influenced by various medical conditions, affecting how the body utilizes energy derived from food. Overall, metabolismo is integral to the health and well-being of living organisms, highlighting the importance of proper nutrition and metabolic function."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}